  "raw_text": "87\n\nKulki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto count, to calculate, to look at accounts, to do accounting, to do an accounting\n \n/ contar,\ncalcular, mirar cuentas, hacer contabilidad, hacer una contabilidad\n\nLaki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto analyze, to examine, to inspect, to evaluate\n \n/ analizar, examinar, inspeccionar, evaluar\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nLaki kaikaia\n \nis similar to\n \nLuki kaikaia\n.\n \nLaki kaikaia\n \ncarries the idea of looking at something while turning it to\nthoroughly examine it whereas\n \nLuki kaikaia\n \nfocuses more on the idea of analyzing something by thinking about it. /\n \nLaki\nkaikaia\n \nes similar a\n \nLuki kaikaia\n.\n \nLaki kaikaia\n \ntiene la idea de mirar algo mientras lo gira para examinarlo a fondo,\n\nmientras que\n \nLuki kaikaia\n \nse centra más en la idea de analizar algo pensando en ello.\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n06/19\n):\n \nAni Baibil smalkanka nani ba laki kaikaia sa yawan miusik walaia plikisa taim?\n \n–\n \nWhat Bible\n\nteachings/principles should we examine when we choose which music to listen to?\n \n/ ¿Qué enseñanzas/principios bíblicos\n\ndebemos examinar cuando elegimos qué música escuchar?\n)\n\nKaisa laki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nlet’s examine\n \n/ examinemos\n\nKli laki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto re-examine, to review\n \n/ reexaminar, repasar\n\nWali nani wal laki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto discuss with others\n \n/ discutir con otros\n\nWali nani wal laki kaikbia\n \n–\n \nAudience Discussion\n \n(the term used for this type of meeting part in\nthe Living as Christians meeting) / Análisis con el auditorio (el término utilizado para este tipo de\nreunión forma parte de la reunión Nuestra Vida Cristiana)\n\nLat lulki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cast lots to see who wins, to cast lots to see what the decision is\n \n/ echar suertes para ver\nquien gana, echar suertes para ver cuál es la decisión\n\nLatan kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto see clearly\n \n/ ver claramente\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-1\n):\n \nWitin nani latan kaikaia sa nahki ai rayaka ra yamni munisa baha tânka aisama ba\n \n–\n \nThey must see clearly\nhow the information that you will tell them does good in their life\n \n/ Deben ver claramente cómo les beneficia en sus vidas\nla información que presentarás)\n\nLatwan kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love, to appreciate\n \n/ amar, apreciar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy51\n):\n \nRut witin ra (Jehova) uba latwan kaikan\n \n–\n \nRuth really loved him\n \n/ Rut realmente lo amaba)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh11\n):\n \nlatwan wan kaiki ba mita,\n…\n \n–\n \nbecause of loving us,\n…\n \n/ por amarnos\n,…\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh42\n):\n \nPana pana latwan tara kaiki kan kaia sa!\n \n–\n \nIt must be that they were loving each other greatly!\n \n/ ¡Debe ser\nque se amaban mucho!)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/20\n):\n \nNaha tasba na yawan latwan kaikbiara\n \n–\n \nWe are not to love this world\n \n/ No debemos amar este\nmundo)\n\nLatwan ai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love me\n \n/ amarme\n\nLatwan mai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love you\n \n/ amarte\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nLatwan mai kaikisna\n \n–\n \nI love you\n \n/ Te quiero\n)\n\nLatwan wan kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto love us\n \n/ amarnos\n\nLuki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto examine, to consider, to imagine, to analyze\n \n/ examinar, considerar, imaginar, analizar\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nLaki kaikaia\n \nis similar to\n \nLuki kaikaia\n.\n \nLaki kaikaia\n \ncarries the idea of looking at something while turning it to\nthoroughly examine it whereas\n \nLuki kaikaia\n \nfocuses more on the idea of analyzing something by thinking about it /\n \nLaki\nkaikaia\n \nes similar a\n \nLuki kaikaia\n.\n \nLaki kaikaia\n \ntiene la idea de mirar algo mientras lo gira para examinarlo a fondo,\n\nmientras que\n \nLuki kaikaia\n \nse centra más en la idea de analizar algo pensando en ello.\n)\n\nAman luki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto examine carefully, to consider carefully, to carefully anal\ny\nze, to meditate\n \n/\n\nexaminar cuidadosamente, considerar cuidadosamente, analizar cuidadosamente, meditar\n\nLuki kaiks!\n \n(a/t:\n \nLuki kais\n)\n \n(\nv\n-\nimp\n)\n \n–\n \nExamine!, Consider!, Imagine!\n \n/ ¡Examina!, ¡\nC\nonsidera!, ¡\nI\nmagina!\n\nMakabi walanka silp luki kaikbia dukiara\n \n–\n \nquestion to analyze yourself, rhetorical question\n \n/\n \npregunta\n\npara autoanalizar\nte\n,\n \npregunta de auto an\ná\nlisis,\n \npregunta retórica\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nth\n-\n3\n):\n \nMakabi walanka dauks upla ba silp luki kaikbia dukiara\n \n–\n \nAsk the person a question for them to\n\nanalyze; Ask a\n \nrhetorical question\n \n/ Hágale una pregunta a la persona para que la analice; Haz una pregunta\n\nretórica\n)\n\nMain kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto mind, to take care of, to watch, to guard\n \n/ cuidar, mirar, proteger\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/18\n):\n \nAlmuk nani ba spirit lainka ra sîp nani ra plun dakakisa, kaina kahbisa bara main kaikisa.\n \n–\n \nElders\nfeed the sheep spiritually, protect, and care for (them).\n \n/ Los ancianos alimentan a las ovejas espiritualmente, las\nprotegen y las cuidan.)\n\nMain ai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto mind me, to take care of me, to watch me, to guard me\n \n/ cuidarme, mirarme,\nprotegerme\n\nMain kaikaia warkka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwork to take care of someone or something,\n \nmaintenance work\n \n(\njl16\n) /\ntrabajo de cuidar a alguien o algo, trabajo de mantenimiento (\njl16\n)",
